---

## Detail per issue

### F1 — Scatter: X / Y axis dropdowns render empty

**Where:** `/#page=scatter` (the Plot view).

**What I see:** The "View" toolbar shows two labelled fields — `X axis` and
`Y axis` — but the dropdowns themselves render as 38 × 28 px containers with
no value, no placeholder, and no clickable affordance. Clicking the labels
does nothing. Inspecting the DOM shows `<div id="scatter-x-col" …></div>`
with no children.

**Impact:** The user cannot start a scatter plot from the Plot view. Only the
heatmap deep-link exposes column choices (and that one is broken too — see F3).

---

### F2 — Scatter empty state blames filters when axes are missing

**Where:** `/#page=scatter`.

**What I see:** "No scatter points found — No points match active filters
(2 column, 0 adaptive)." This appears the moment the user lands on the page,
because no axes are selected. The phrase "(2 column, 0 adaptive)" is
confusing — it suggests "2 columns" are filtered, when the real reason is
"no axes".

**Impact:** First-time users think their data is broken or filtered. They
have no idea they need to pick X and Y.

---

### F3 — Heatmap-to-Scatter deep link drops X/Y

**Where:** `/#page=correlations` → click any heatmap cell.

**What I see:** Clicking HULL × MULL (0.91) navigates to
`#page=scatter`. The scatter page then shows the same empty state from F2 —
X and Y are not pre-populated, no chart is drawn, and Pearson/Spearman
remain `—`.

**Impact:** The single most discoverable path into scatter is broken.

---

### F4 — Timeseries Y-axis shows negative range for positive data

**Where:** `/#page=timeseries`.

**What I see:** Default Y ticks read `-15.20, 16.80, 48.80, 80.79, 112.79`,
but every series in the dataset is strictly positive (oil temperatures in
`HUFL/HULL/MUFL/MULL/LUFL/LULL/OT`). About 25 % of vertical space is wasted
on empty area below zero.

**Impact:** Charts feel "broken" — values look negative, vertical resolution
for the actual data range is wasted.

---

### F5 — Robust y-range controls visible while disabled

**Where:** `/#page=timeseries` → `Y range` group.

**What I see:** When "Hide spike-driven span" is unchecked, both
`Mode (Percentile)` and `Param (1)` remain visible but greyed out. New users
see what looks like three active controls when only one is actually wired up.

**Impact:** Suggests the page is in a half-configured state. Users waste time
trying to interact with disabled controls.

---

### F6 — Series chips duplicate the in-chart legend

**Where:** `/#page=timeseries`.

**What I see:** Two places list the same series names:
- The "Series" toolbar at the top has chips for HUFL, HULL, … OT.
- The chart's corner legend inside the SVG also lists the active series.

There is no obvious link between the two; they can drift apart.

**Impact:** Cognitive overhead. The in-chart legend also lacks the per-series
"Set … color" controls that the toolbar chips have, so users have to learn
which affordance lives where.

---

### F7 — Adaptive filter hint banner has no docs link

**Where:** `/#page=timeseries` → "Ctrl + click a selected series to add an
adaptive line filter" banner.

**What I see:** The banner shows a hint and a dismiss "×". There's no link to
documentation, and the "?" tooltip in the Draw group mentions adaptive filters
only in passing. The hint is shown by default for every new dataset, even
when the user already knows the feature.

**Impact:** Onboarding value is small; experienced users dismiss it every
time they reload.

---

### F8 — FFT for slow signals collapses to a single near-DC point

**Where:** `/#page=fft` with ETTm2 (HUFL, HULL selected).

**What I see:** The plot shows a single red dot at `0.02 µHz (725.8 days)`,
with the X axis stretching from `0` to `~0.0006 µHz`. The two chips are
clearly pressed (HUFL + HULL), but the chart looks empty because the actual
signal energy sits at much higher frequencies.

**Impact:** Looks like the FFT engine is broken when in reality the chosen
display window does not match the signal's frequency content. The
"Top peaks 0.02 µHz · 0.06 µHz · 0.05 µHz" annotation is not visible without
hover and is easy to miss.

---

### F9 — FFT Clip controls visible while disabled

**Where:** `/#page=fft` → `Display` group.

**What I see:** "Clip method" + "Clip %" remain in the toolbar with the
disabled styling when "Outliers" is unchecked. Same pattern as F5.

---

### F10 — "Computing FFT…" copy never clears

**Where:** `/#page=fft` main panel.

**What I see:** After Compute finishes, the text "Computing FFT…" still
appears overlaid on the chart area. Possibly only visible on first paint,
but easy to read as "still computing".

---

### F11 — Spectrogram silently picks HUFL

**Where:** `/#page=spectrogram`.

**What I see:** Lands already loaded with HUFL selected and a spectrogram
rendered. There's no toast / banner explaining "we picked HUFL because it
was first", and no obvious way to know the chosen column if you weren't
looking at the dropdown.

**Impact:** Nice auto-default, but invisible to the user — feels like magic
on revisit, and accidental on first sight.

---

### F12 — Causal pre-selects variables but shows an empty graph

**Where:** `/#page=causal`.

**What I see:** HUFL, HULL, OT chips are highlighted as selected, but the
graph area is empty until Compute is pressed. The summary stats panel on the
right is also empty. Users who don't read the "Compute" button label will
think the page is broken.

**Impact:** Same family of issue as F8 — page looks empty despite being
"ready".

---

### F13 — Causal header is dense and tooltips-heavy

**Where:** `/#page=causal` top toolbar.

**What I see:** "ALGORITHM Method PCMCI · Test ParCorr · τ max 3 · α 0.05 ·
PC α 0.2 · Max conds auto · FDR None" all on one row, with a `?` tooltip
on almost every field. Scrolling with the eye is hard.

**Impact:** Power users can deal with it; first-time users bounce.

---

### F14 — Drift "Columns" button hides multi-select

**Where:** `/#page=drift` → `Data` group.

**What I see:** A single button labelled "HUFL" suggests a single choice.
Clicking opens a panel; there is no chip group visible inline. Most users
will assume the page is single-column.

**Impact:** The "Columns" naming also doesn't match the chip-style selectors
used on the Timeseries and Spectrogram pages.

---

### F15 — Drift status bar sticks on pre-compute copy

**Where:** `/#page=drift` status banner.

**What I see:** After pressing Compute and getting results, the banner still
reads "Select one or more columns, choose a baseline, and press Compute."
above a result table that shows drift detected.

**Impact:** Confusing state — message contradicts the rendered output.

---

### F16 — Drift "Composite PSI + Wass + KS + E-S" is jargon-only

**Where:** `/#page=drift` → `Thresholds` group.

**What I see:** A group whose only label is "Composite PSI + Wass + KS + E-S".
No tooltip, no expansion, no plain-language explanation.

**Impact:** Power users will understand, but new users have no idea what a
threshold group does.

---

### F17 — Correlations metric dropdown header is split

**Where:** `/#page=correlations` top toolbar.

**What I see:** Eyebrow label is `METRIC`, but the dropdown field next to it
uses `TYPE` as its column label, with its own `?` tooltip. The two compete
for visual attention.

**Impact:** Minor but adds noise to a small toolbar.

---

### F18 — Correlations cell-size value rendering

**Where:** `/#page=correlations` → `Display` group.

**What I see:** Slider with value `36` shown both to the right of the label
"Cell size" and as a slider thumb position. The number is rendered in a
way that looks like a separate field rather than a slider readout.

**Impact:** Minor; the pattern works but the visual emphasis is ambiguous.

---

### F19 — Upload filter row reads like two competing filter sets

**Where:** `/#page=upload` → `File preview` header.

**What I see:** Two pill groups side by side: `All / None` and
`All / Numeric / Datetime`. The first toggles "include selected" vs
"include none", the second filters by column type. New users read this as
two ways to do the same thing.

**Impact:** The `None` button is easy to miss because it sits at the same
visual weight as `All`, and the meaning of the two pairs is not labelled.

---

### F20 — Date column profile truncates timestamps

**Where:** `/#page=upload` profile grid, `date` row.

**What I see:** `Min` and `Max` cells show `2016-07-01T00:00:…` and
`2018-06-26T19:45:…`. The full timestamp is not visible without hovering;
users cannot tell whether the data is 15-minute or daily.

**Impact:** Minor; affects trust in the preview.

---

### F21 — Guided workflow "✓ 4 completed" sticks

**Where:** top banner on most pages after `/#page=scatter`.

**What I see:** After clicking through Scatter, the workflow strip auto-opens
saying "✓ 4 completed" and offers "→ Scatter" / "Open Causal" actions. The
count includes pages the user only briefly visited, and the workflow stays
visible until manually hidden.

**Impact:** Suggests the user did more than they did. The strip also
overlaps the page toolbar and the user's chart on small screens.

---

### F22 — Disabled controls share enabled styling

**Where:** global.

**What I see:** Disabled comboboxes and spin-buttons keep the same border,
background, and padding as enabled ones. Only the chevron and the cursor
change. They look like normal inputs that just don't respond.

**Impact:** F5, F9 and F15 all stem from this.

---

### F23 — Settings "Density" label

**Where:** `Settings → Appearance → Layout`.

**What I see:** Field is labelled `Density`, with options
`Spacious / Roomy / Compact`. No `Layout` prefix, no tooltip.

**Impact:** Minor; label alone doesn't tell the user this is about UI density.

---

### F24 — Home sample-data cards: ambiguous next-step badges

**Where:** `/#page=home`.

**What I see:** Each sample card has two badges:
- a category badge (`Time-series`, `FFT`, `Correlations`)
- a hint badge (`Best first stop: Timeseries`)

The first is a *topic tag*, the second is a *recommended next page*. They
look identical at a glance.

**Impact:** Mild onboarding friction; could be unified.

---

### F25 — Empty chart states don't tell the user what to do

**Where:** Scatter, Causal, Drift, FFT (before Compute).

**What I see:** When the chart area is empty, the placeholder copy says
what is missing ("Select columns", "Pick a column and click Compute") but
not which toolbar control to click. The action lives one screen away.

**Impact:** New users bounce. This affects F1, F2, F8, F11, F12, F14.

---

# Plan of fixes

Each fix below is sized to fit inside one focused PR. Order: F1 / F3 first
(scatter is unusable today), then F4 / F8 / F12 (broken-looking charts),
then F22 + everything that flows from it (F5 / F9 / F15), then the polish
batch.

### Fix 1 — Render the scatter X / Y axis dropdowns (F1)

**Goal:** Make X-axis and Y-axis pickable so the scatter page actually
renders.

**Shape:**
- Audit the dropdown component used for `scatter-x-col` /
  `scatter-y-col`. It's the same `data-dropdown-id` component used
  elsewhere; the symptom is that on the Scatter page the option list is
  not hydrated.
- Likely root causes to check:
  - The scatter page receives `numericColumns` only after a metadata
    fetch completes; if the dropdown mounts before that fetch resolves,
    it renders empty. Solution: re-hydrate the dropdown after
    `datasetState.numericColumns` is populated, or render the dropdown
    only once `numericColumns.length > 0`.
  - The dropdown's option-builder may key off `categoricalColumns` /
    `numericColumns` separately and miss the scatter case. Verify the
    numeric-column source.
- Add a regression test: load the ETTm2 sample, navigate to
  `#page=scatter`, assert `scatter-x-col` contains 7 options and a
  default selection of `HUFL`.

**Acceptance:**
- `scatter-x-col` and `scatter-y-col` show 7 column options each.
- Both have sensible defaults (e.g. `HUFL` / `HULL`) so first-time users
  see a populated chart.
- The empty state copy disappears once defaults are set.

---

### Fix 2 — Re-word the scatter empty state when axes are missing (F2)

**Goal:** Tell the user why the chart is empty and what to do.

**Shape:**
- Distinguish three empty reasons: (a) no axes picked, (b) axes picked but
  filters return zero rows, (c) data fetch failed.
- When (a): replace the message with "Pick an X and Y column above to plot
  your data." and put a button "Open X axis" that scrolls to / focuses
  the `scatter-x-col` dropdown.
- When (b): keep the existing message but drop "(2 column, 0 adaptive)"
  jargon — just say "No points match the active filters."
- When (c): surface the API error message inline with a retry button.

**Acceptance:**
- Loading `/api/scatter/points` with empty body returns no error but no
  rows; the UI shows the (a) state.
- After clicking "Open X axis", the X-axis dropdown receives focus.

---

### Fix 3 — Make heatmap → scatter deep-link set X and Y (F3)

**Goal:** Clicking a heatmap cell should land the user on Scatter with the
right axes pre-selected and the chart rendered.

**Shape:**
- Confirm where the deep-link navigation happens (heatmap cell click
  handler). Today it sets `page=scatter` only.
- Pipe the clicked (row, col) pair into `scatterState.xColumn` /
  `scatterState.yColumn` before navigation.
- Persist the selection in the URL hash (`#page=scatter&x=HULL&y=MULL`) so
  it survives reloads and the share-link path. Use the same parser the
  URL-hash fix in Fix 1 will rely on.
- Trigger an initial `/api/scatter/points` fetch as soon as both axes are
  known — do not wait for a manual "Compute" that doesn't exist on the
  Scatter page.

**Acceptance:**
- Click HULL × MULL on the heatmap → Scatter loads with X=HULL, Y=MULL,
  Pearson/Spearman stats populated, density backdrop rendered.
- Browser URL hash reflects the selection.

---

### Fix 4 — Y-axis auto-fit for strictly-positive data (F4)

**Goal:** Timeseries Y-axis should hug the data, not include empty bands.

**Shape:**
- When computing the default Y range, compute per-series min/max (across
  the active chips and within the current viewport) and floor the lower
  bound to `min(0, globalMin)` instead of `0` always and
  `min - 5 %` always.
- Also: enable "Pin lower bound" by default when **all** active series are
  non-negative, and disable it when any series goes negative.
- Add a small `toolbar-field__helper` line under the Y-range group
  explaining when the floor is pinned.

**Acceptance:**
- ETTm2 default view shows Y range ~5 → 120, no negative ticks.
- If a user selects a series with negative values, the floor relaxes
  automatically.

---

### Fix 5 — Hide disabled controls until their parent toggle is on (F5, F9, F22)

**Goal:** Disabled controls should not be visible.

**Shape:**
- Replace the "show-but-greyed" pattern with conditional rendering:
  - "Mode" + "Param" only render when "Hide spike-driven span" is on.
  - "Clip method" + "Clip %" only render when "Outliers" is on.
  - Same for FFT filter Low/High Hz — only render when Filter Type ≠ Off.
- Where the toggle has dependent controls, render them in a subtle inset
  panel to make the relationship obvious.
- Add a small `aria-disabled` / `disabled` on the parent toggle for
  accessibility.

**Acceptance:**
- ETTm2 default Timeseries view shows Y-range with two fields, not four.
- Switching the toggle on reveals the dependent fields with an animation.

---

### Fix 6 — De-duplicate series chips and in-chart legend (F6)

**Goal:** One source of truth for the active series list.

**Shape:**
- Hide the in-chart SVG legend and keep the toolbar chips as the
  single interactive surface.
- Or, if the in-chart legend is required for accessibility, keep it but
  remove the toolbar chips' selection state and leave only color +
  visibility controls in the toolbar. Series visibility becomes a click
  on the in-chart legend.

**Acceptance:**
- The same series name only appears once in the active UI.
- The per-series "Set … color" affordance stays.

---

### Fix 7 — Adaptive-filter hint banner (F7)

**Goal:** Onboarding hint should be useful and unobtrusive.

**Shape:**
- Move the hint to the first time a user opens a dataset — dismiss it
  forever after that.
- Add a docs link "Learn more" pointing at the timeseries help page.
- Persist the dismissed state in `localStorage` so it doesn't reappear
  on reload.

---

### Fix 8 — FFT: auto-pick a frequency window that matches the data (F8)

**Goal:** FFT should show useful content for slow signals like ETTm2.

**Shape:**
- On first render of an FFT page, run a quick "find dominant frequency"
  pass and auto-zoom the X axis to a band of `0.1 × … 10 ×` the dominant
  frequency.
- Surface the dominant frequency and the chosen band as a small caption
  under the chart so users understand why the axis starts where it does.
- Add an "Auto-fit" toggle (default on) so users can disable it.
- If the user has manually zoomed, do not auto-reset until they press
  the existing "↺" zoom reset button.

**Acceptance:**
- ETTm2 with HUFL selected shows a populated FFT band, not a single DC
  dot.

---

### Fix 9 — Clear stale "Computing FFT…" copy (F10)

**Shape:**
- Wrap the FFT rendering pipeline so that the "Computing…" overlay is
  unmounted as soon as the response is parsed. Currently it appears to
  remain in the DOM after `state.status === 'ready'`.

